# The public address the deployed frontend and eBay's registration both name.
#
# NOT an Elastic IP. `aws ec2 describe-addresses --public-ips 35.173.35.240`
# answers InvalidAddress.NotFound, so this is the instance's ephemeral public
# address: a stop/start, an instance replacement or an AWS maintenance event
# gives the box a different one.
#
# Four things name it, and an IP change breaks all four at once:
#
#   the frontend      VITE_API_BASE, a Vercel environment variable, baked into
#                     the bundle at build time — so a change needs a rebuild and
#                     a redeploy, not just a setting
#   the TLS name      Caddy holds a certificate for <ip-with-dashes>.sslip.io
#   eBay OAuth        the redirect registered against the app's RuName
#   eBay deletion     EBAY_DELETION_ENDPOINT, registered with eBay verbatim and
#                     a compliance requirement they enforce
#
# `scripts/deploy-aws.sh` compares the live address against this file on every
# deploy and refuses when they differ, because the deploy would otherwise stand
# up a NEW hostname, report success, and leave the frontend calling the old one.
35.173.35.240
